; chains.kurt
;
; relations chained on one line, `a = b ≤ c`, mean `a = b and b ≤ c` -- and chained
; across continuation lines, each continuation line concludes from the first line's LHS
load arith
calc on                     ; `calc` checks comparisons of literal numbers, e.g. `3 ≤ 4`

2 + 1 = 3 ≤ 4
5 = 2 + 3 ≤ 7 < 8
10 = 5 + 5
   ≤ 12
   < 13
10 < 13

; parentheses keep the plain reading: `(2 = 3) ≤ 4` compares a boolean with a number,
; which no axiom (and no calculation) says anything about
expect "ProofError"
    (2 = 3) ≤ 4
; a false link breaks the whole chain
expect "ProofError"
    2 = 3 ≤ 4

; with constants: one chained line gives each link, and transitivity combines two of them
calc off
use a = b ≤ c < d
a = b ≤ c
a ≤ c
